    "title": "Recall alert: Xanax recalled nationwide",
    "text": "The Food and Drug Administration has announced the nationwide recall of the anti-anxiety medication Xanax. The agency said the recall affects a single lot, 8177156, which expires on 02/28/2027.The recall occurred because the pills failed dissolution specifications, the FDA said.The recalled Xanax came in 3 mg pills with the bottles containing 60 tablets. They were distributed by Viatris Specialty of Morgantown, West Virginia. They were produced in Ireland and have NDC number 58151-506-91. The pills were distrubuted in the U.S. from Aug, 27, 2024 to May 29, 2025, the California State Board of Parmacy said in a news release.They were initially recalled on March 17, but the recall was classified as a Class II on April 8. A Class II recall is “a situation in which use of or exposure to a violative product may cause temporary or medically reversible adverse health consequences or where the probability of serious adverse health consequences is remote,” the FDA said.Latest recalls:Recall alert: 94K Hyundai vehicles recalled over fuel leakRecall alert: 1.39M Ford F-150s recalled; may downshift without warningRecall alert: 440K Honda Odyssey minivans recalled; air bags may deploy unexpectedlyRecall alert: 25K Magic Pocket Staffs recalled, can cause cutsRecall alert: 149K generators recalled; can catch fire©2026 Cox Media Group",
